  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.0.0 - BREAKING. Two breaking changes. `Log.Logger` compiles unchanged, and `ExcludePaths` does for configuration-only hosts, while code that reads `ExcludePaths` sees `string[]?`. `AddStepUpLogging` no longer assigns Serilog's static `Log.Logger`, and disposing the host no longer calls `Log.CloseAndFlush()`, so each host logs through its own DI logger (#31); the step-up and step-down warnings now go through the bypass logger instead of `Log.Warning`, and the step-down warning now exports even when `BaseLevel` is above Warning - migrate static `Log.*` callers to DI `ILogger<T>`, or set `SetStaticLogger = true` to restore the old behavior. A configured `ExcludePaths` now replaces the built-in defaults (`/healthz`, `/metrics`, `/health`) instead of being appended to them, and an explicit `[]` excludes nothing (#32) - list the defaults in your configuration to keep them, and in code assign the whole list, since the property is `null` inside `configureOptions` unless configuration sets it. Added: `CategoryFloors` sets a per-category minimum level by `SourceContext` prefix, with `DiagnosticExemptCategories` keeping a floor during Diagnostic mode. `AlwaysExportCategories` exports matching categories once at any level through the immediate path (#35). `NeverTriggerCategories` names categories whose errors do not trigger step-up, and `sink_error_events_total` now counts only errors that requested a step-up trigger, so errors from these categories are not counted (#35). `Mode = Diagnostic` holds the switch at `DiagnosticLevel` for `DiagnosticDurationMinutes` at startup, then runs as Auto, and lifts the `NeverStepUpCategories` pin for that window, so EF `Database.Command` SQL is exported for the whole window - pin that category with `CategoryFloors` plus `DiagnosticExemptCategories` (#35). A new `AddStepUpLogging` overload takes both the options callback and the `(IServiceProvider, LoggerConfiguration)` callback (#35). `RedactLogEventProperties` opts in to applying `RedactionRegexes` to string and URI-like properties of application log events (#20, #34). Fixed: `RedactionRegexes` now reaches the request path in the summary, the request event and the `LogRequest` span (#30). The pre-error buffer exports every event at most once and drops held-back events at shutdown (#29). The encrypted spool's delivery client no longer inherits `ConfigureHttpClientDefaults` resilience handlers, and adds a dependency on `Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience` (#33). See CHANGELOG.md and MIGRATION.md.",
